Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::a_chain_describes_its_bytes_inside_the_region`.

The defect: the last descriptor holds a whole page whatever is left, so a transfer that is not a
whole number of pages describes more bytes than the command moves, and the IDMAC waits on a
descriptor the card will never fill.

Expected to fail: `assert!(i * PAGE + size == bytes)`, on any `bytes` that is not a multiple of a page.

diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/idmac.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/idmac.rs
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/idmac.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/idmac.rs
@@ -214,7 +214,7 @@
     } else {
         des0 |= DES0_DIC;
     }
-    let size = if last { bytes - i * PAGE } else { PAGE };
+    let size = PAGE;
     let next = if last { 0 } else { i + 1 };
     [
         des0,
